---
import CommonContent from "~/components/CommonContent.astro";
import { articles } from "~/data/articles";
import { links } from "~/data/links";
import ArticleLayout from "~/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout article={articles["volunteer-guide"]}>
	<Fragment slot="lead">
		This page has the high-level information you need to know as a volunteer at
		SquiggleConf.
	</Fragment>

	<Fragment slot="intro">
		<p>That includes:</p>

		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href="#volunteer-expectations">Volunteer Expectations</a>: what we
				need from you before and during
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="#volunteer-schedule">Volunteer Schedule</a>: the schedule of
				activities common to all volunteers
			</li>
		</ul>
	</Fragment>

	<CommonContent heading="Volunteer Expectations">
		<p>Volunteers are required to:</p>

		<ul>
			<li>
				Attend a volunteer training and orientation in-person Thursday evening
			</li>
			<li>
				Be available and responsive on the <a
					href={links.discord}
					target="_blank">SquiggleConf Discord</a
				> for the duration of the two conference days
			</li>
		</ul>

		<p>
			We generally assign an equal number of task hours to each volunteer,
			roughly (number of hours of work) / (number of volunteers). Those tasks
			will generally be in-person work such as operating the help desk, guiding
			attendees to lunch spots, and helping set up and take down equipment.
		</p>

		<p>We'll also need the following information from you:</p>

		<ul>
			<li>Preferred first and last name</li>
			<li>Preferred time availabilities midday Wednesday through Friday</li>
			<li>Photo: at least 512x512px</li>
			<li>Specifics on any accessibility, dietary, or other needs</li>
			<li>Which talks you most want to be free to attend</li>
		</ul>

		<p>Volunteers must be in-person for the duration of the conference.</p>
	</CommonContent>

	<CommonContent heading="Volunteer Schedule">
		<p>
			Volunteers are invited to all public conference events. We'll post the
			full schedule closer to May 2027.
		</p>
	</CommonContent>
</ArticleLayout>
